WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.333
Andy, how are you?

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:02.307
I'm good.

00:00:02.307 --> 00:00:05.020
I wanna bring up something
here at the top of the show

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.840
because Andy Richter sits
by my side every night

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.240
and I've grown very fond of you Andy,

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.115
in the last two...
Are you firing me?

00:00:12.115 --> 00:00:13.000
(Conan chuckles)
(audience laughing)

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:13.833
No.

00:00:15.588 --> 00:00:16.421
Oh, okay.
Not at all.

00:00:16.421 --> 00:00:17.780
Not at all Andy.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.460
Why are you so paranoid?

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.293
I don't know.
No I have,

00:00:20.293 --> 00:00:22.440
I've become very fond of
you over the three seasons

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.780
we've been doing this show,

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.310
and I've gotten to know
Andy better and better.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.560
But actually a couple of
weeks ago, I said to Andy,

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.240
'You know, I really wanna know
the Andy before I knew him.'

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.030
I wanted to go and explore
the roots of Andy Richter,

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.570
the humble beginnings.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.460
And Andy said, 'Well,
if you wanna do that,

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.250
I should take you Conan to my
old neighborhood in Chicago.'

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.083
Right.

00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.170
And show you around.

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.003
And we did.

00:00:46.003 --> 00:00:47.240
And we did that,
Just that.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.140
and we brought a camera crew.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.410
And I gave you sort of

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.720
it's the Andy Richter tour of Chicago.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.810
It's not in any books.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:54.643
That's right.

00:00:54.643 --> 00:00:56.203
This is a different look
at the city of Chicago.

00:00:56.203 --> 00:00:58.565
Right.
All Andy Richter.

00:00:58.565 --> 00:00:59.760
Its within about a three block radius.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.593
Okay.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.716
And...

00:01:01.716 --> 00:01:02.549
Well, this is exciting stuff actually.

00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:05.070
And we're gonna show
the whole world tonight,

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:05.903
your beginnings.

00:01:05.903 --> 00:01:07.870
Where you come from and
Andy Richter, Chicago.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:08.703
Great.

00:01:08.703 --> 00:01:09.850
So ladies and gentlemen lets take a look

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:12.430
at Andy's and Mike tour

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.440
around his old neighborhoods in Chicago.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.273
Enjoy.

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:19.117
(classical music)

00:01:27.236 --> 00:01:30.236
(audience laughing)

00:01:32.913 --> 00:01:34.121
(classical music)

00:01:34.121 --> 00:01:37.598
[Mike] This is great.
[Andy] Yeah, It's cold.

00:01:37.598 --> 00:01:40.340
Yeah, this was a good
idea though, to come here.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:45.340
I mean, and sit in Wrigley
field in the dead of winter.

00:01:46.232 --> 00:01:49.065
(audience laughs)

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.740
Nothing funny about it?

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:54.573
No.

00:01:55.431 --> 00:01:58.264
(classical music)

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:10.220
This is the intersection of
Lincoln Irving park and Damon.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.093
Okay.

00:02:11.093 --> 00:02:11.926
It is sort of the heart
of the neighborhood

00:02:11.926 --> 00:02:13.900
that I used to live in.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.500
And there's no better place to start

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:16.610
than the Lincoln restaurant.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.550
Wow!

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.890
It's sort of like my home away from home.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:21.730
Wait a minute.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:22.680
This is a--

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.513
Oh my God.

00:02:23.513 --> 00:02:24.593
I love Chicago.

00:02:24.593 --> 00:02:26.110
(laughs)

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:27.230
[Andy] Here we go.
Thank you.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.063
That looks terrific.

00:02:28.063 --> 00:02:30.296
That's the veal cutlet Parmesan?

00:02:30.296 --> 00:02:31.193
Yep.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.540
There we go.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.660
Omelette and a skillet.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:35.712
Yeah.

00:02:35.712 --> 00:02:36.586
(audience laughs)

00:02:36.586 --> 00:02:38.890
Well, here we are this is Alvin Glick.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:39.723
Cool.

00:02:39.723 --> 00:02:41.070
I used to live here.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.050
This is pretty much where you spent two

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.460
or three consecutive
years of your life, right?

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:46.310
Pretty much.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.108
Listen and we like a couple of beers

00:02:48.108 --> 00:02:50.850
(bartender) sure what would you like?

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.708
What kind of beer do you want first?

00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:56.030
Something German but we
brought our own glasses.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.783
Yeah, can you fill it and these actually?

00:02:58.783 --> 00:02:59.616
Sure, I can do that.

00:02:59.616 --> 00:03:00.836
I hope these people have a urinal.

00:03:00.836 --> 00:03:02.380
There we go.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.963
(upbeat music)

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:31.280
Andy, what's that thing on your head?

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.980
It's an inflatable bears helmet.

00:03:33.953 --> 00:03:35.387
Please take it off.

00:03:36.273 --> 00:03:39.106
(classical music)

00:03:40.118 --> 00:03:42.895
(audience laughing)

00:03:42.895 --> 00:03:45.728
(classical music)

00:04:03.625 --> 00:04:06.625
(audience laughing)

